        "original_id": "2b76ff96-8264-542d-b568-33e510eb59fb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Graham Linehan, Arthur Mathews, Ash Atalla, Chris O'Dowd, Richard Ayoade, Katherine Parkinson, Matt Berry, Steven Toast\n- TV Series: Father Ted, Black Books, The IT Crowd, Hippies, Toast of London\n- Organizations: Channel 4\n- Roles: writer, producer, creator, actor, character\n\nFacts:\n- Graham Linehan is most noted for the sitcoms Father Ted, Black Books, and The IT Crowd.\n- The IT Crowd is a British sitcom by Channel 4 written by Graham Linehan, produced by Ash Atalla, and starring Chris O'Dowd, Richard Ayoade, Katherine Parkinson, and Matt Berry.\n- Hippies was created by Arthur Mathews and Graham Linehan, whose writing partnership is most famous for Father Ted, but the scripts for Hippies were written by Arthur Mathews alone.\n- Toast of London is a British comedy television series created by Arthur Mathews and Matt Berry.\n- Matt Berry stars in Toast of London as Steven Toast, an eccentric middle-aged actor with a chequered past who spends more time dealing with problems off stage than performing.",
